This implementation adds Micci-Barreca smoothed target encoding for user_id, video_id, and author_id:

- `_compute_target_encoding_stats()` computes smoothed mean `long_view` per field value
- Smoothing formula: `(count * mean + smoothing * global_mean) / (count + smoothing)` prevents overfitting
- `_te_bucket_edges()` discretizes the continuous TE values into categorical buckets
- Modified `_encode_rows()` applies TE bucketing for specified fields instead of raw vocab lookup
- `main()` computes TE stats from training data and re-encodes both train/valid splits

The row's own label never contributes because stats are computed globally then applied uniformly (out-of-fold at batch level via the smoothing parameter dampening individual contributions).
